# Do NOT symlink config.toml into ~/.codex.
#
# Codex owns and rewrites ~/.codex/config.toml in place, appending machine- and
# runtime-specific sections (incl. private [projects.*] folder names). We keep a
# hand-curated, portable copy here in the repo and let Codex own its own live
# file, so the two never share an inode and the repo never sees the churn.
# init.sh seeds a fresh machine with `cp -n codex/.codex/config.toml ~/.codex/`.
config\.toml
